The `add_dirty()` function (pager.rs lines 2917-2934) performs both operations atomically under locks:

```rust
pub fn add_dirty(&self, page: &Page) -> Result<()> {
    turso_assert!(page.is_loaded(), ...);
    self.subjournal_page_if_required(page)?;
    let mut dirty_pages = self.dirty_pages.write();  // Lock acquired
    dirty_pages.insert(page.get().id as u32);        // Insert into bitmap
    if !page.is_dirty() {
        let key = PageCacheKey::new(page.get().id);
        self.page_cache.write().notify_page_dirty(key);
    }
    page.set_dirty();                                 // Set flag
    Ok(())
}
```

The dirty_pages bitmap uses RoaringBitmap (line 1302) which is efficient for sparse sets. The insert and set_dirty happen within the same function call, ensuring both are done together.

