The commit flow (pager.rs lines 3529-3554) uses `dirty_pages` as the authoritative source:

```rust
CommitState::ScanAndIssueReads { db_size } => {
    let dirty_pages = self.dirty_pages.read();

    if dirty_pages.is_empty() {
        return Ok(IOResult::Done(()));
    }
    commit_info.initialize(dirty_pages.len() as usize);

    for page_id in dirty_pages.iter() {
        let page_id = page_id as usize;
        let page_key = PageCacheKey::new(page_id);
        if cache.peek(&page_key, false).is_some() {
            commit_info.page_sources.push(PageSource::Cached(page_id));
        } else {
            // Page was evicted, re-read from WAL
            let (page, completion) = self.read_page_no_cache(page_id as i64, None, false)?;
            commit_info.page_sources.push(PageSource::Evicted(page));
        }
    }
}
```

The commit iterates `dirty_pages.iter()` and processes every page ID in the bitmap. Even if a page was evicted from cache (spilled to WAL earlier), it's still in `dirty_pages` and will be re-read for the final commit.
